Value Required INTERFACE (Eth-Trunk\d+)
Value GROUP (\d+)
Value PROTOCOL (\S+)
Value List MEMBERS ([A-Za-z][\w/.-]*\d)
Value List MEMBER_FLAGS (\S+)
Value List BUNDLED ([A-Za-z][\w/.-]*\d)

# One record per Eth-Trunk in LACP mode (eNSP Pro USG6306F and CE6800, YunShan OS
# 1.25.1.1): its local ports with their LACP status; a Selected port is bundled (read
# twice through a lookahead). The flags after a port name ((h), (r)) are not modeled; the
# partner rows (a priority where the status is) are skipped. A manual (NORMAL) trunk
# prints another table, not verified yet.
Start
  ^\d{4}-\d\d-\d\d \d\d:\d\d:\d\d(?:\.\d+)?\s*$$
  ^Eth-Trunk\d+'s state -> Continue.Record
  ^${INTERFACE}'s state information is:\s*$$
  ^\((?:h|r)\):.*$$
  ^(?:Local|Partner):\s*$$
  ^LAG ID:.*Working Mode:\s*NORMAL.* -> Error "manual Eth-Trunk format not verified"
  ^LAG ID:\s*${GROUP}\s+Working Mode:\s*${PROTOCOL}\s*$$
  ^(?:Preempt Delay|System Priority|Least Active-linknumber|Operating Status|Timeout Period|PortKeyMode|Hash Arithmetic):.*$$
  ^-+\s*$$
  ^ActorPortName\s+(?:Status\s+PortType|SysPri\s+SystemID).*$$
  ^(?=${BUNDLED}(?:\([a-z]+\))?\s+Selected\s)${MEMBERS}(?:\([a-z]+\))?\s+${MEMBER_FLAGS}\s+\S+\s+\d+\s+\d+\s+\d+\s+\d+\s+\d+\s*$$
  ^${MEMBERS}(?:\([a-z]+\))?\s+${MEMBER_FLAGS}\s+\S+\s+\d+\s+\d+\s+\d+\s+\d+\s+\d+\s*$$
  ^\S+\s+\d+\s+[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}\s+\d+\s+\d+\s+\d+\s+\d+\s*$$
  ^\s*$$
  ^. -> Error "unrecognized display eth-trunk line"
